---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = 'August 8, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Maxxtopia"
  description="How Maxxtopia and its apps, extensions, and games handle your data. Short version: we collect as little as possible and never sell it."
>
  <article class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8 pt-24 pb-24 prose-legal">
    <p class="text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-[var(--color-magenta)] font-mono">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-[36px] sm:text-[52px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] leading-[1.02] gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-white/50">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6 text-white/75 leading-relaxed text-[15px]">
      <p><strong class="text-white">The short version.</strong> Maxxtopia builds free, local-first tools. We collect as little data as possible, we don't sell it, we don't run third-party ad trackers, and most of our software runs entirely on your own device.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Who we are</h2>
      <p>"Maxxtopia" ("we", "us") operates the website <a href="https://maxxtopia.com">maxxtopia.com</a> and a suite of apps, browser extensions, and games, including the <strong class="text-white">Sprite Cannon</strong> Twitch Extension. Contact: <a href="mailto:dtman@maxxtopia.com">dtman@maxxtopia.com</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Sprite Cannon (Twitch Extension)</h2>
      <p>Sprite Cannon is a play-while-you-watch game that runs as an overlay on a streamer's channel. It collects only what's needed to run a per-channel leaderboard:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><strong class="text-white">A display name you choose</strong> when you submit a score (you type it; it does not have to be your real name).</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">Your best distance score</strong> for that play session.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">The Twitch channel ID</strong> of the stream you're playing on, so your score posts to that streamer's leaderboard.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This data is stored on Cloudflare infrastructure and shown publicly on the in-game leaderboard by design. We do <strong class="text-white">not</strong> request or store your Twitch identity (the extension does not use Twitch Identity Linking), we do <strong class="text-white">not</strong> read Twitch chat, and we do <strong class="text-white">not</strong> collect email, payment, or location data. There are no ads and no third-party advertising or analytics trackers inside the extension.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Desktop apps</h2>
      <p>Our desktop apps are local-first: your media, settings, and accounts stay on your device. Where an app offers optional usage telemetry, it is <strong class="text-white">off by default</strong> and anonymous when enabled.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Streammaxxing and YouTube data</h2>
      <p>Streammaxxing offers an optional <strong class="text-white">Connect YouTube</strong> feature for its unified chat overlay. The integration requests the read-only <code>youtube.readonly</code> permission only after you choose to connect your Google account.</p>
      <p>When connected, Streammaxxing accesses only the YouTube data needed to find and display your live chat:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><strong class="text-white">Your YouTube channel ID and channel name</strong>, so the app can identify the channel you connected.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">Your active live-broadcast and live-chat identifiers</strong>, so the app can detect when you go live and connect automatically.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-white">Live-chat messages and their public author details</strong>, so messages can appear in the local Streammaxxing chat and OBS overlay.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Streammaxxing does <strong class="text-white">not</strong> request your Google password or email address, and it cannot upload, edit, or delete videos; manage playlists or subscriptions; or post as you.</p>
      <h3 class="text-white text-lg font-semibold pt-2">Security and protection of Google user data</h3>
      <p>We use encryption and other technical safeguards to protect the Google user data handled by Streammaxxing. Google OAuth and YouTube API requests use HTTPS. Access tokens are held in memory while the app uses them. Before the refresh token, connected channel ID, and channel name are written to disk, Streammaxxing encrypts them with the Windows Data Protection API (DPAPI), scoped to the signed-in Windows user. The encrypted data is stored only in Streammaxxing's local Windows app-data folder, and Google OAuth tokens are not sent to Maxxtopia servers.</p>
      <p>Streammaxxing validates the OAuth callback state before accepting a Google authorization. Live-chat messages are processed locally and are not retained by Maxxtopia or sent to Maxxtopia servers. If you add the chat overlay to OBS, you intentionally choose to display those messages on your broadcast. The <strong class="text-white">Forget Google link</strong> revokes the saved authorization and deletes the encrypted local credential file.</p>
      <p>We do not sell, share, advertise against, profile from, or use Google user data to train generalized AI or machine-learning models. Our use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>
      <p>You can stop YouTube access in Streammaxxing with <strong class="text-white">Forget Google link</strong>, which revokes the saved Google authorization and removes the local encrypted token files. You can also revoke access from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">Google Account connections</a>. Uninstalling Streammaxxing stops access; use Forget Google link or Google Account connections first if you also want the saved authorization revoked.</p>
      <p>Google and YouTube process data under their own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a>. Questions about Streammaxxing's YouTube integration: <a href="mailto:streammaxxing-support@googlegroups.com">streammaxxing-support@googlegroups.com</a>.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Website</h2>
      <p>maxxtopia.com is a static site hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Standard server logs (such as IP address and request metadata) may be processed by our hosting provider to deliver and secure the site. We do not place advertising cookies.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">How we use data</h2>
      <p>Only to provide the feature you're using (e.g., showing leaderboard scores) and to keep our services secure and working. We do not sell or rent your data to anyone.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Retention &amp; your choices</h2>
      <p>Leaderboard entries persist so scores can be displayed and ranked. To have a leaderboard entry removed, email <a href="mailto:dtman@maxxtopia.com">dtman@maxxtopia.com</a> with the channel and the name you used and we'll remove it. You can stop all data collection at any time by not submitting a score / uninstalling the extension or app.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Children</h2>
      <p>Our products are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Third parties</h2>
      <p>When you use the extension on Twitch, Twitch's own <a href="https://www.twitch.tv/p/legal/privacy-notice/">Privacy Notice</a> also applies to your use of Twitch. Our infrastructure runs on Cloudflare.</p>

      <h2 class="text-white text-xl font-semibold pt-4">Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy; material changes will be reflected by the "Last updated" date above.</p>

      <p class="pt-4">Questions? <a href="mailto:dtman@maxxtopia.com">dtman@maxxtopia.com</a>.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm"><a href="/legal/terms" class="text-[var(--color-cyan)]">Terms of Service →</a></p>
  </article>
</Layout>
